<title>TURKEY: Turk c bank fx reserves up $519 mln last week.</title>
<headline>Turk c bank fx reserves up $519 mln last week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on</p>
<p>Thursday its foreign currency reserves rose by $519 million to</p>
<p>$16.215 billion in the week ended on August 30.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>			 Aug 30	  Aug 23	   end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve     16.215	  15.696	   12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve	 1.383	   1.383	    1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve     17.598	  17.079	   13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose $73 million to $26.849 billion in the week ending August 16, the bank said.</p>
<p>It said Turkey had serviced $81.44 million of state foreign debt in the first three days of this week.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
